Plugin clarification

fastforwardrs is licensed under the GNU General Public License, version 3 or (at your
option) any later version (see the file LICENSE).

The copyright holder of fastforwardrs, John Dorsey, states that a program or file (a
"plugin") which fastforwardrs loads at run time, and which works with fastforwardrs only
through an interface that is published for plugins (at the time of writing: LADSPA, CLAP,
ISF and .cube), is not, merely because fastforwardrs loads it and calls it, a work based on
fastforwardrs, and need not be licensed under the GPL: its authors may license it as they
choose, free or not.

This clarification does not apply to a plugin that contains code copied from
fastforwardrs, that is linked into fastforwardrs's own executable, or that uses
fastforwardrs's internal (unpublished) interfaces; and it gives no permission to copy,
modify or distribute fastforwardrs itself on any terms other than those of the GPL.

A project file that contains a plugin is a collection of separate works, each under its own
licence.

